docs/public/day-analysis-2026-02-17.html:395:  <p>B2 wrote 51 adversarial tests for its own relay system — including replay attacks, lease expiry races, injection attempts, and chain tampering. Test-then-ship, not ship-then-hope. The adversarial suite validates every QWRR invariant (I1-I5). When an agent can red-team itself, the human can trust the green output.</p>
docs/public/day-analysis-2026-02-17.html:405:  <p>B2's <code>ops/sandbox/</code> directory received 5 new files today (~2,200 lines): local_relay.py, cross_model_dialogue.py, event_replay.py, policy_engine.py, secrets_contract.py. None of these were in the backlog. All emerged from the Idle Protocol's "Architect" mode. The sandbox pattern — zero production risk, full creative freedom — turned spare capacity into five production-ready prototypes. Three of them (policy engine, secrets scanner, observability) shipped to production within hours of being invented.</p>
